{"content":[{"c":["FRANKINCENSE"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Fragrant gum resin that can be ground into powder and burned to produce a balsamlike odor. It was often associated with myrrh (",{"href":"?bref=Song.3.6","r":"Song.3.6","rawR":"Song.3.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Song.3.6","value":"Song.3.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Sg 3:6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Song.4.6","r":"Song.4.6","rawR":"Song.4.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Song.4.6","value":"Song.4.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"4:6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.2.11","r":"Matt.2.11","rawR":"Matt.2.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.2.11","value":"Matt.2.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 2:11"},"). Frankincense is obtained from balsam trees of the genus ",{"c":["Boswellia,"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," specifically the species ",{"c":["B. carterii, B. papyrifera,"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," and ",{"c":["B. thurifera."],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," These trees, which are related to turpentine trees, have star-shaped flowers that are pure white or green, tipped with rose. To obtain the resin, a deep incision is cut into the trunk, yielding an amber-colored gum. Since these trees were native only to Saba (Sheba) in southern Arabia (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.60.6","r":"Isa.60.6","rawR":"Isa.60.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.60.6","value":"Isa.60.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 60:6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.6.20","r":"Jer.6.20","rawR":"Jer.6.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.6.20","value":"Jer.6.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 6:20"},") and Somaliland, the resin was a costly item transported into Palestine by caravan. The so-called frankincense tree growing in Palestine (",{"href":"?bref=Ecclus.50.8","r":"Ecclus.50.8","rawR":"Ecclus.50.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ecclus.50.8","value":"Ecclus.50.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ecclus 50:8"},") was probably ",{"c":["Commiphora opobalsamum"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," whose resin was used to produce perfume."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["Frankincense was used alone or with other materials for incense. It was one of the ingredients of the holy incense used for worship in the tabernacle (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.30.34","r":"Exod.30.34","rawR":"Exod.30.34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.30.34","value":"Exod.30.34"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 30:34"},"). It was placed on the bread of the Presence (",{"href":"?bref=Lev.24.7","r":"Lev.24.7","rawR":"Lev.24.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.24.7","value":"Lev.24.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lv 24:7"},") and mixed with oil on the cereal offerings (",{"href":"?bref=Lev.2.1-2,14-16","r":"Lev.2.1-2,14-16","rawR":"Lev.2.1-2,14-16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.2.1-2,14-16","value":"Lev.2.1-2,14-16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lv 2:1-2, 14-16"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Lev.6.15","r":"Lev.6.15","rawR":"Lev.6.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.6.15","value":"Lev.6.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"6:15"},"), but it was excluded from the sin offering (",{"href":"?bref=Lev.5.11","r":"Lev.5.11","rawR":"Lev.5.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.5.11","value":"Lev.5.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:11"},"). A supply of frankincense was maintained in the Jerusalem temple (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.13.5,9","r":"Neh.13.5,9","rawR":"Neh.13.5,9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.13.5,9","value":"Neh.13.5,9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 13:5, 9"},"). It was later used in cosmetics and perfume (",{"href":"?bref=Song.3.6","r":"Song.3.6","rawR":"Song.3.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Song.3.6","value":"Song.3.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Sg 3:6"},"). Both the costly value and its use for worship made the presentation of frankincense to the infant Jesus an appropriate gift (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.2.11","r":"Matt.2.11","rawR":"Matt.2.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.2.11","value":"Matt.2.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 2:11"},"). ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Plants_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Plants_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Plants_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Plants"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Frankincense","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Sg 3:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Song.3.6","rawQueryValue":"Song.3.6","sourceRefExact":"Song.3.6"},{"anchorText":"4:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Song.4.6","rawQueryValue":"Song.4.6","sourceRefExact":"Song.4.6"},{"anchorText":"Mt 2:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.2.11","rawQueryValue":"Matt.2.11","sourceRefExact":"Matt.2.11"},{"anchorText":"Is 60:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.60.6","rawQueryValue":"Isa.60.6","sourceRefExact":"Isa.60.6"},{"anchorText":"Jer 6:20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.6.20","rawQueryValue":"Jer.6.20","sourceRefExact":"Jer.6.20"},{"anchorText":"Ecclus 50:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ecclus.50.8","rawQueryValue":"Ecclus.50.8","sourceRefExact":"Ecclus.50.8"},{"anchorText":"Ex 30:34","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.30.34","rawQueryValue":"Exod.30.34","sourceRefExact":"Exod.30.34"},{"anchorText":"Lv 24:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Lev.24.7","rawQueryValue":"Lev.24.7","sourceRefExact":"Lev.24.7"},{"anchorText":"Lv 2:1-2, 14-16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Lev.2.1-2,14-16","rawQueryValue":"Lev.2.1-2,14-16","sourceRefExact":"Lev.2.1-2,14-16"},{"anchorText":"6:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Lev.6.15","rawQueryValue":"Lev.6.15","sourceRefExact":"Lev.6.15"},{"anchorText":"5:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Lev.5.11","rawQueryValue":"Lev.5.11","sourceRefExact":"Lev.5.11"},{"anchorText":"Neh 13:5, 9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.13.5,9","rawQueryValue":"Neh.13.5,9","sourceRefExact":"Neh.13.5,9"},{"anchorText":"Sg 3:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Song.3.6","rawQueryValue":"Song.3.6","sourceRefExact":"Song.3.6"},{"anchorText":"Mt 2:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.2.11","rawQueryValue":"Matt.2.11","sourceRefExact":"Matt.2.11"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"078de77b403b17ac9dfd9a04d6e324bd096f494edfb45b439441c15d69562b21","sourceItemName":"Frankincense","sourceItemOrder":78,"sourceMember":"Articles/F.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Frankincense","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Frankincense","title":"Frankincense","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}